      },
      "text": "OSPF lab. R1 and R2 already run OSPF in area 0; R3 doesn't, so PC1 can't reach PC3. Open the OSPF view (View menu or the OSPF tab) as you go. 1) On R3: router ospf 1, router-id 3.3.3.3, network 0.0.0.0 255.255.255.255 area 0, passive-interface g0/3. Check show ip ospf neighbor and ping PC3 from PC1. 2) On R1 Gi0/2 set ip ospf cost 10 and see the route to 192.168.3.0/24 move to R2. 3) Right-click the R1\u2013R2 cable, Fail Link (OSPF View), and step through the reconvergence."
